<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 38 GATE 5c, AC 18. THE FIRST TIME THE WEBDAV CONNECTOR IS DRIVEN
  FROM INSIDE THE APP. Gate 4 unit-tested SWebDavClient / SWebDavMediaSource
  against the stub and said so plainly (gate 4 AC 9: "at the end of gate 4 the
  WebDAV client is unit-tested and has never been driven from the app"); gate 5b
  built the accounts model that can point one at a URL. This case is where the
  two meet: a real SMediaAccountManager account, a real SWebDavMediaSource in
  SMediaRegistry, the real SMediaBrowserPanel, and PROPFINDs going over a real
  TCP socket - driven by the gate-2 verbs, UNCHANGED, which is the claim AC 18
  actually makes.

  HOW THIS CASE LEARNS THE PORT. It does not, and it must not. The stub binds
  127.0.0.1:0 - an OS-assigned port, never a fixed one, which is exactly what
  stops four concurrent `ctest -j4` cases colliding over it - and a .qxa is a
  static document that cannot interpolate a run-time value into a later
  attribute. So `media-webdav-stub` writes the URL where the rest of the flow
  reads it: given accountId=, it calls SMediaAccountManager::setAccount()
  ITSELF, with the stub's own baseUrl(). From here this case names only the
  SOURCE ID, "nextcloud:qxastub", which is static. See the verb's header for the
  two alternatives that were considered and are worse.

  THE STUB SERVES THE COMMITTED FIXTURE TREE, REAL BYTES AND ALL
  (smaragd/tests/media/, mirrored by fixtureDir="../media/lib"):

      kick.wav          768044 bytes (a byte copy of test_sawtooth.wav)
      snare.wav         768044
      notes.txt         73      the thing the Audio filter must omit
      sub/hat.wav       768044
      sub/deep/tom.wav  768044

  That is the SAME tree media_browser_browse.qxa walks through the LOCAL
  provider, and that is deliberate: every row count and every "name,size,isDir"
  triple below is identical to the local case's, so a difference between the two
  providers shows up as a diff between two nearly identical files rather than as
  a number nobody can check. The sizes are the fixture's own bytes and a
  directory's size is the documented -1 ("unknown").

  WHAT IT PINS

  1. An account pointed at the stub becomes a source. `media-browser-source
     sourceId="nextcloud:qxastub"` succeeds, which it can only do when
     SMediaRegistry holds that id - and the source combo is rebuilt from that
     same registry list on every sourcesChanged, with selectSource() setting its
     current index by findData(). (The combo's ROWS are not in describe(), so
     what is asserted here is the registry membership the combo is built from,
     not the widget's item list. Stated rather than implied.)
  2. Browsing the root over PROPFIND: three rows under the Audio filter,
     directories first, notes.txt absent - and present again with an empty mask,
     which is the positive control without which "absent notes.txt" would also
     pass on a browser that showed nothing at all.
  3. LAZY EXPAND over the wire: expanding `sub` issues its own depth-1 PROPFIND
     and expanding `deep` inside it issues another, so the laziness is not a
     one-level special case. Then an explicit path, which collapses back.
  4. SEARCH over the wire - the client-side breadth-first walk of depth-1
     PROPFINDs (§B.7: search is deliberately client-side, so a server answering
     SEARCH with a 501 cannot break it). Recursive finds every .wav in the tree
     ("a" is in ".wav"); non-recursive finds the two directly in the root; a
     directory is never a result however well its name matches.
  5. THE CREDENTIAL REACHES THE WIRE, BYTE FOR BYTE. Every PROPFIND below is
     made against a stub that demands `Basic cXhhdXNlcjpxeGFwYXNz` - the base64
     of `qxauser:qxapass`, the exact pair `media-webdav-stub` handed to
     SMediaAccountManager::setAccount() - and answers 401 to anything else. So
     every green row count above is also a statement about the bytes in the
     Authorization header, not merely about the PROPFIND parser. The literal is
     spelled out rather than derived: deriving it would be a second copy of
     SMediaAccountManager::basicHeader() checking itself.

     Item (6) is its NEGATIVE CONTROL, and it is not optional - without it a
     stub that silently ignored expectAuth= would pass every assertion in this
     file, which is precisely the failure gate 6 exists to close.

  6. A SERVER FAULT IS A BANNER, not an empty folder. The stub is told to answer
     500 for `sub`, the panel browses there, and the inline banner (§B.4) comes
     up with zero rows; clearing the fault and browsing back clears it. The
     assertion is on the banner FLAG and the row count, not on the message text
     - the wording comes from Qt's own network error string and is not this
     repo's to pin.

  WHAT IS NOT PINNED HERE, and it matters more than usual:

   * THE STUB IS NOT A NEXTCLOUD SERVER. Plain HTTP: no TLS (so no certificate
     validation and no TLS-error surfacing), no redirects, no rate limiting and
     no WWW-Authenticate challenge; one canonical PROPFIND dialect, not
     Nextcloud's. All of that is the manual runbook's job (§C.6,
     docs/MEDIA_BROWSER_MANUAL_GATE.md).

     What it DOES check since gate 6 is the credential - see (6). Gate 5c
     shipped without that and its own PR body named the hole: the chain
     SSecretStore -> smedia::CredentialProvider -> SWebDavClient's header ->
     the wire was exercised end to end and never verified, because the stub
     would have served these same files just as happily for an empty header.
   * Pixels. The panel is built off screen and never shown (trap T10);
     describe() is the oracle and paintEvent is not exercised.
   * The 401-does-not-retry rule, the mid-body close, the in-flight cap and the
     truncation bound: gate 4's unit test owns all four, against the same stub.

  SETTINGS OWNERSHIP (trap T6). RUN_SERIAL. This case OWNS
  media/lastSourceId, media/lastPath/nextcloud:qxastub, media/categoryMask,
  media/searchRecursive, and every key under media/nextcloud/qxastub/*. It
  restores the first four to their SOpt defaults and removes the account, so
  smaragd.ini comes back with identical CONTENT. (CONTENT, not md5: QSettings
  rewrites the whole file from its own in-memory map and does not promise to
  preserve section ORDER across processes, so an md5 can legitimately move while
  every key is exactly as it was.) media/lastSourceId is shared with the four
  other RUN_SERIAL media cases and every one of them restores it to "local".
  SMARAGD_SECRET_BACKEND=memory is set explicitly by the CTest entry rather than
  inherited: the account only has to work for THIS process, and `memory` writes
  no INI key and no keychain item at all.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="media_webdav_browse">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- Defensive: a previous run that died mid-script cannot have left a
         server behind (the process is gone), but it could have left the
         account's url/user keys. -->
    <remove-media-account accountId="qxastub"/>

    <!-- (1) The stub, the fixture tree, and the account - one verb, because the
         port only exists once the server is listening. -->
    <media-webdav-stub accountId="qxastub" fixtureDir="../media/lib"
                       user="qxauser" password="qxapass" remember="0"
                       expectAuth="Basic cXhhdXNlcjpxeGFwYXNz"/>
    <!-- The account IS in the model the source combo is built from. No
         accountCount= here on purpose: this INI is the developer's own and
         may legitimately hold their real accounts too. -->
    <assert-media-options contains="qxastub"/>

    <media-browser-filter categories="audio"/>
    <media-browser-source sourceId="nextcloud:qxastub" waitMs="10000"/>

    <!-- (2) The root, over PROPFIND. Identical to media_browser_browse.qxa's
         local listing, on purpose. -->
    <assert-media-browser mode="browse" rowCount="3"
                          contains="|source=nextcloud:qxastub|"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="|filter=audio|"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="sub,-1,1"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="kick.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="snare.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser absent="notes.txt"/>
    <!-- Nothing was truncated and nothing failed: a bound is ANNOUNCED
         (app/media inv. 4), so its absence has to be assertable too. -->
    <assert-media-browser truncated="0" contains="|banner=0|error="/>

    <!-- The positive control for the line above. -->
    <media-browser-filter categories="" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="4" contains="notes.txt,73,0"/>
    <media-browser-filter categories="audio" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="3" absent="notes.txt"/>

    <!-- (3) LAZY EXPAND, two levels, each its own depth-1 PROPFIND. -->
    <media-browser-path expand="sub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="5" contains="hat.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="deep,-1,1"/>
    <media-browser-path expand="deep" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="6" contains="tom.wav,768044,0"/>

    <!-- (4) SEARCH: the client-side breadth-first walk, from the root. -->
    <media-browser-search needle="a" recursive="1" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser mode="search" rowCount="4"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="kick.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="tom.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser absent="notes.txt"/>
    <!-- A DIRECTORY is never a result, however well its name matches. -->
    <assert-media-browser absent="sub,-1,1"/>

    <media-browser-search needle="a" recursive="0" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser mode="search" rowCount="2"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="snare.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser absent="hat.wav"/>
    <assert-media-browser absent="tom.wav"/>

    <!-- An empty needle returns to BROWSE at the same path, which is still the
         root - the ROOT IS ONLY REACHABLE THIS WAY, because setBrowsePath()
         refuses an empty spelling and a WebDAV root IS the empty path. -->
    <media-browser-search needle="" recursive="1" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser mode="browse" rowCount="3"/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="kick.wav,768044,0"/>

    <!-- ...and an explicit remote path collapses to one directory's worth. -->
    <media-browser-path path="sub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser mode="browse" rowCount="2"
                          contains="hat.wav,768044,0"/>
    <assert-media-browser absent="kick.wav"/>

    <!-- (5) A 500 from the server is a BANNER, not an empty folder. Re-listing
         the SAME path is what re-issues the PROPFIND: setBrowsePath() has no
         same-path early-out, on purpose (it is what the Retry button rides on). -->
    <media-webdav-stub fault="500" faultPath="sub"
                       expectAuth="Basic cXhhdXNlcjpxeGFwYXNz"/>
    <media-browser-path path="sub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="0" contains="|banner=1|"/>

    <!-- ...and an empty fault= restores the healthy server in one line.
         expectAuth= is repeated because it is NOT sticky either: one
         invocation states the server's whole state. -->
    <media-webdav-stub fault="" expectAuth="Basic cXhhdXNlcjpxeGFwYXNz"/>
    <media-browser-path path="sub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="2" contains="|banner=0|error="/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="hat.wav,768044,0"/>

    <!-- (6) THE NEGATIVE CONTROL FOR THE CREDENTIAL. The server is told to
         demand base64("qxauser:wrong") instead; the account still holds
         "qxapass", so the header the client actually sends no longer matches
         and every PROPFIND comes back 401. A WRONG PASSWORD IS A VISIBLE
         FAILURE, not a silent pass - which is the assertion that stops a stub
         ignoring expectAuth= from making every row count above vacuous. It
         also pins that the PASSWORD is compared and not merely the presence
         of a header: the two spellings share their first eleven base64
         characters, the encoding of the "qxauser:" half. -->
    <media-webdav-stub expectAuth="Basic cXhhdXNlcjp3cm9uZw=="/>
    <media-browser-path path="sub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="0" contains="|banner=1|"/>

    <!-- ...and the right credential brings the listing straight back. A 401 is
         reported ONCE and nothing retries (§B.7), so there is no session state
         to clear here - which is itself worth pinning. -->
    <media-webdav-stub expectAuth="Basic cXhhdXNlcjpxeGFwYXNz"/>
    <media-browser-path path="sub" waitMs="10000"/>
    <assert-media-browser rowCount="2" contains="|banner=0|error="/>
    <assert-media-browser contains="hat.wav,768044,0"/>

    <!-- Tear the server down explicitly rather than leaving it to teardown. -->
    <media-webdav-stub action="stop"/>

    <!-- Restore every key this case owns (T6). -->
    <remove-media-account accountId="qxastub"/>
    <assert-settings-file absent="nextcloud\qxastub\"/>
    <set-option key="media/lastSourceId" value="local"/>
    <set-option key="media/lastPath/nextcloud:qxastub" value=""/>
    <set-option key="media/categoryMask" value="1"/>
    <set-option key="media/searchRecursive" value="false"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="0"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
